content.text:
Yes—the reported problem was primarily **wrong guidance**, not failure to honor a correctly configured non-origin remote.

The CLI told users to set `checkpoint_remote`, omitted the required nesting, and led them to `"checkpoint_remote": "entire"`. They needed:

```json
{
  "strategy_options": {
    "checkpoint_push_remote": "entire"
  }
}
```

Our reproductions confirm that this correct setting works. **#2327 fixes that misleading hint.**

The routing edge cases we found are separate issues; I broadened the investigation beyond the original report.

